# PlaylistPlaybackRecommendationLiveness 1

The system owns continuous playlist playback: after a playable current track
finishes, a recommendation producer may still be computing the next track.
The player must not convert that temporary empty frontier into a finished
session. First-slot preparation remains a generation-stamped cross-domain
preparation owner; its cached credentials, startup warmup, invalidation, and
consumption lifecycle are not replaced by the normal queue planner.

## Domain `architecture`

```Forma
PlaylistSession = Construction
  (CurrentTrack `P` OrderedQueue `P` RecommendationProducer)
FirstSlotCargo = Construction
  (PlaylistScope `P` PreparedSource `P` Generation `P` Credential)
QueueObservation = Construction (Playing `S` Preparing `S` Finished)

observe_queue :: PlaylistSession `AR` QueueObservation
advance_recommendation :: RecommendationProducer `TR` PreparedContinuation
consume_first_slot :: FirstSlotCargo `TR` StartupQueue
```

The player consumes an explicit queue. The playlist owner supplies
recommendations and owns candidate-scope materialization. First-slot cargo is
an independent preparation path and must preserve its cross-domain state and
linear credential consumption.

## Behavior `architecture`

```Forma
queue_liveness =
  Transport
    advance_recommendation
    observe_queue
    PreparedContinuation

temporary_frontier_gap =
  MissingNext `P` RecommendationWork `P` NotTerminal

producer_terminal =
  ProducerTerminal `TR` Finished

first_slot_continuity =
  Transport
    consume_first_slot
    observe_queue
    StartupQueue
```

An open playlist queue remains in `Preparing` while the producer is working.
Only an explicit producer terminal may emit `Finished`; an ordinary ordered
queue retains its existing finite-session terminal behavior. A stale producer
result cannot mutate a superseded session.

## Performance `architecture`

```Forma
materialize_scope =
  Work MaterializePlaylistScope CandidateWindow Iteration 1

reuse_scope =
  Memoize MaterializePlaylistScope

successor_frontier =
  Work AdvanceSymbolicProgram PreparedContinuation Iteration 1

queue_observation =
  Work observe_queue SessionObservation Iteration 1

recommendation_frontier =
  Work advance_recommendation PreparedContinuation Iteration 1

first_slot_consumption =
  Work consume_first_slot StartupQueue Iteration 1

scope_reuse_invalidated =
  Invalidates PlaylistMembershipChanged CandidateWindow
```

The stable symbolic program is evaluated over a materialized playlist scope.
Repeated successor steps in one unchanged generation reuse that materialized
scope instead of reloading the complete library window. Playlist, exclusion,
download, file-availability, or model-generation changes invalidate the
reused scope; this is a correctness boundary, not a tuning parameter.

## Search `search`

```Forma
required =
  TemporaryFrontierGapNotTerminal
  `P` ExplicitProducerTerminal
  `P` FirstSlotCacheCompatibility
  `P` BoundedSuccessorWork

forbidden =
  CacheRestoreFailureDiscardsPreparedCargo
  `S` QueueProducerStillWorking
  `S` PermanentOrderedTerminal

search_order =
  Lexicographic
    LifecycleOwnership
    CrossDomainStatePreservation
    MaterializedScopeReuse
    IndependentValidation

search_budget =
  BranchBudget 8 1
```

The search space includes lifecycle, representation, and ownership repairs.
The observed 19-second track followed by a 30-second recommendation is a
counterexample to treating queue exhaustion as a terminal without a producer
receipt. The old `audio_style` first-slot cache tag is a compatibility input,
not permission to discard the entire prepared pool.

## Implementation `architecture`

The queue policy belongs to `player::service` session state, while the
playlist queue producer owns the terminal receipt and symbolic scope reuse.
`playlist_playback::playable_index` remains the sole owner of first-slot
cache restore, generation stamping, invalidation, and credential consumption.

```text
@forma implements enum PlaylistPlayableIndexSourceKind as src-tauri/src/domain/playlist_playback/playable_index.rs
@forma summary accepts the legacy audio_style cache tag while writing the canonical symbolic_program tag
@forma implements function run_playback_session as src-tauri/src/domain/player/service.rs
@forma summary keeps an open playlist queue preparing until its producer signals terminal
@forma implements method AudioStyleSymbolicPlaybackSession::propose_next as src-tauri/src/domain/playlist_playback/recommendation.rs
@forma summary reuses an unchanged generation-owned materialized symbolic scope
@forma implements method AudioStyleSymbolicPlaybackSession::observe_scope_revision as src-tauri/src/domain/playlist_playback/recommendation.rs
@forma summary invalidates the materialized scope when the playable-index revision changes
@forma implements function mark_session_queue_terminal as src-tauri/src/domain/player/service.rs
@forma summary makes producer termination an explicit player-owned lifecycle receipt
```

